# Round q38tier (ntier piece 7): Qwen3.8 at --place bp, plan (b′): the A6000 as under plan (a) with the 3090 as its
# expert tier, against --place a, same binary, the shipped defaults otherwise (residency, the MTP draft and host
# streaming unset: mid-p120-s1, mtp, on). Phase 2a put the tier on the decode walks, phase 2b (q38tier2b) on the
# prompt's ubatch walk, its rows packed by rank and copied by the 3090's copy engine. The tier pays on the prompt,
# so the card's one term is the prompt at P = 4096; P = 512 and the drafted pass are read beside it.
#
# [functional, q38tier2b, same binary, not admissible] Per layer-batch from `stat prompt lb` / `split`
# (BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1, prose ids, both cards in view; target/q38tier/func2b/split2.log, one window), ms:
#                front  down  shadow  upload  back | host union | pp tok/s
#   a  P 4096    30.27  1.93   22.61   13.10  0.25 |      26.74 | 1,225
#   bp P 4096    30.48  1.92   16.93    6.44  0.25 |       7.50 | 1,483
#   a  P 512      2.97  0.24    6.94    1.04  0.04 |       6.59 |   933
#   bp P 512      2.98  0.25    3.95    1.11  0.04 |       3.39 | 1,250
# The card stream is the wall, a sum of its five spans; the host union runs under it in both arms. The tier takes
# ~4,200 slots a layer at P 4096 (10.2 %) and ~650 at P 512. Three ways for the tier's rows were run (functional):
# zero-copy stores into the host-mapped rows (1,229 / 1,222 at P 4096 / 512: the 3090's mapped writes run at
# ~1.9 GB/s, 43 MB in ~23 ms a layer, and the A6000 idled behind them), the port's whole 419 MB copy (1,345 at
# P 4096: the copy engine moves ~23.5 GB/s), and the tier's rows packed by rank and copied alone (43 MB, ~1.8 ms:
# the leg ends under the host union, settle ~0.4 ms a call; upload = the joint sum's mapped reads ~4.7 + the host
# sums' 1.6). The engine keeps the packed path alone.
#
# [derived, the term, P 4096] bp's layer: front 30.5 + down 1.9 + shadow 16.9 + upload 6.4 + back 0.25 = 56.0 ms
# against a's 68.2 (its upload span waits for the 26.7 ms host union): 48 x 56.0 + 25 = 2,713 ms against 3,298:
# +21.5 %; the functional pair read +21.1 %. Band +15..+28: the functional rows' window (no lease, no rotation; a's
# 1,225 here against rig-log's admissible 1,224) and the shadow's and the joint sum's spread (+-2 ms a layer).
# [derived, P 512, read beside] 8.33 against 11.23 ms a layer: +34 % (functional +34.0 %), +25..+40.
# Not taken: the tier's packed rows copied into the A6000 under its shadow (the joint sum from device memory,
# 0.6 ms): upload 6.4 -> ~2.2, ~1,600 at P 4096 [derived]; it needs a device buffer for the packed rows on the
# A6000 (up to every slot, 419 MB at U 4,096, or a bound with the mapped read past it) and a copy stream joined
# before the sum.
# The drafted pass's block below is Phase 1's derivation with Phase 1's counts; the plan now holds the A6000 at
# 242/241 a layer (11,610), the tier at 150/151 (7,236) and the host at 119/120 (5,730) (qwen4exp_mtp_meta's
# BP_DRAFTED): the A6000 −72 to the tier join's rows, the tier −68 to its run rows, both near the ids' boundaries.
#
# [derived, the drafted pass, read beside] The split (place::machine_bp; qwen4exp_meta BP_PLAIN, qwen4exp_mtp_meta BP_DRAFTED): both cards plan to
# their budgets, the A6000 keeping plan (a)'s drafted row (244/243 a layer, 11,682 at 4k), the 3090 the next ids
# (150/151 a layer, 7,229), the host the rest (118/119, 5,665). Residency holds the tier's ids away, so the tier's
# routed share is its ids' mass, about 150.6 / 512 = 29.4 % under the id prefix, whatever the A6000 keeps.
# Term by term on a drafted pass (window: the draft's chain + a verify of E(4) rows; rig-log 10-01#q38head-ab,
# 37.43 ms at P 512, 37.06 ms at P 4096; slots a layer 10 x E(4): 36.9 at P 512, 31.0 at P 4096):
# - the A6000's card slots. Plan (a)'s residency serves 83.5 % of the mass on 244 of 512 ids at P 4096 and 70.2 %
#   at P 512 (rig-log 10-01#q38hol-ab: 246 / 527 host slots a pass). A concentration curve 1 - (1 - x)^a fitted
#   there (a 2.78 / 1.87) puts the A6000's top 243.6 of the 361.4 non-tier ids at 95.6 % / 87.8 % of their 70.6 %:
#   67.5 % / 62.0 % of the mass, so its slots fall 25.9 -> 20.9 (P 4096) and 25.9 -> 22.9 (P 512) a layer,
#   at 3.072 MB an expert and 575 GB/s (5.3 us a slot): -1.28 ms and -0.77 ms a pass. Band from the curve's
#   shape (the A6000 loses 12..20 points of mass): -0.95..-1.6 ms at P 4096, -0.6..-1.0 ms at P 512.
# - the tier's leg: 9.1 / 10.8 slots a layer at 4.4 us (3090, 700 GB/s), with its go wait, three copies in and
#   its signal about 60..70 us a layer, under the A6000's leg of about 120 us: 0.
# - the host leg: under the A6000's at P 4096 in both arms (0). At P 512 plan (a)'s host leg shows by about 0.8 ms
#   a pass (the two P's passes differ by 0.37 ms while P 4096's attention reads about 0.4 ms more); under bp the
#   host's share falls 29.8 % -> 8.6 %, 11.0 -> 3.2 slots a layer, under the A6000's: -0.8 ms at P 512.
# - the handoff and the join: the tier's places and q8_1 activation in the same handoff launch, the tier's go and
#   wait in the existing mem-op batches (no node), the card sum reading 9..11 tier rows of 10 KB a layer through
#   the mapping: +0.2..+0.5 ms a pass; up to +1.0 ms if each mapped access pays the per-node floor the pass's
#   15 ms residue suggests (q38two2).
# - dense, KV, head, the MTP chain: unmoved.
# Net: P 4096 -1.4..-0.45 ms of 37.06 (-3.8..-1.2 %); P 512 -2.4..-0.4 ms of 37.43 (-6.4..-1.1 %). Band for both
# P: -6.5..-1, their union with the edge nearest 0 rounded out to -1. The term is signed as card.py reads it:
# below the band is a larger saving than predicted, above it a smaller one (or none). This is below the spec's
# +5..+10 % decode: that figure balanced the two cards' slots as if they were freely assignable, which needs the
# hot ids on the tier (a frequency list, retired, or tier-slot residency, a swap.rs design question).
#
# Why the drafted pass is read beside the term in ms and not as tok/s: the tier computes its experts on card kernels
# where plan (a) ran them on the host's AVX2 union, so the target's bits move at near ties and the greedy text parts
# (q38hol-ab and q38head-ab parted at tokens 72 / 8 for smaller moves); E(4) then mixes into tok/s. The pass is read
# from each arm's `time pass` rows of kind=mtp, warm passes left out; tok/s and E(4) beside it. The prompt term has
# no such mix: one prompt call's wall over the same ids in both arms.
# The P 512 legs above come from runs at the default ctx 4096; the sitting runs at 4352, where the drafted plan
# holds ~2 fewer stage experts (11,608 against 11,610 in the functional plan lines): inside the band.
#
# Runner (lead; the full output to a file first). Two gaps close first: tools/ref/depth-qwen3moe.sh takes one
# BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE for every ours arm and refuses bp, so it needs a per-arm place (e.g. `prose:4096@place=bp`) in
# the load key; and the timing runner pins TIMING_GPU to the A6000 alone, so a bp arm needs both cards in view with
# the 3090 at its 250 W cap and the Xid witness before and after (AGENTS.md: the A6000+3090 table). Then:
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38tier-ab.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512 prose:4096 prose:512@place=bp prose:4096@place=bp
# Rounds: sd 1.0 %, from q38seed-mtp's same-binary MTP pairs; 4 rounds give h ~1.7 %, the band's edge 15 far past it.
# Wall [derived]: 2 load groups x 4 rounds = 8 Qwen3.8 loads with the draft (31-49 s each), the two prompts
# (0.4 + 2.8 s) and 2 x 96 tokens a load: 6-9 min.
kind: ab
question: does plan (b′) — the 3090 as the A6000's expert tier, holding each layer's next ~151 ids, serving the
  prompt's ubatch walk through the batch port with its rows packed and copied by its copy engine — raise Qwen3.8's
  prompt throughput at P = 4096 by the host union it takes off the card's path?
term: prompt tok/s (time prompt rows, kind=gemm) @ prose:4096, one ubatch of 4,096, ctx 4352, A6000 + 3090, --place
  bp against --place a, residency, draft and host streaming unset (mtp), same binary, paired by round; prose:512's
  prompt tok/s (+25..+40) and both P's drafted pass ms read beside
unit: %
predict: +15..+28
rounds: 4
sd: 1.0 % q38seed-mtp's same-binary MTP pairs (rig-log 09-30#q38seed-ab, 6 rounds, +-1.3 % / +-0.9 %); the prompt's
  own scatter is not measured, and the band's nearest edge sits far past this ruler
condition: one binary, every arm in one lease, a fresh process per load group, the order rotated every round, the
  host set and the PLE table warm, no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row, no Xid in either witness, the 3090 at 250 W;
  the a arms' plan line names place=a and no tier, the bp arms' place=bp tier=3090 with tier_experts within 48 of
  the plan's; both arms' load draft=mtp, residency unset mid-p120-s1 and the prompt kind=gemm; each arm's prompt
  tok/s, tokens line, mtp summary E(4) and pass time read beside
decide-in: the packed rows hold under the lease: write the rows (pp tok/s at 512 and 4096, pass ms, tok/s, E(4)) to
  rig-log's A6000+3090 table and price the A6000-side copy of the packed rows under the shadow (~1,600 at P 4096
  [derived]) as the next prompt lever
decide-below: the prompt gained less than the packed path's functional rows: one BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 run of each
  arm at P 4096 (the upload span, the union, gate_qwen38_twocard's settle wait) to name the leg before any change
decide-above: a's P 4096 row is slower under the lease than its functional 1,225 (the host union binds harder):
  re-read a's stat prompt lb rows before reading the gain as the tier's
